    "# DiscoveryBench \u2014 NLS-SES analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question**: Is the relation between socioeconomic status and chances of\n",
    "degree completion affected by racial lines of the individual?\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook reproduces `analysis.py` (the executed script in\n",
    "`/workspace/analysis.py`) and produces the artifacts in `/workspace/outputs/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run cells in order.  Source data: `/workspace/data/nls_ses_processed.csv`\n",
    "**n = 8,773 rows, 8 columns, no missing values**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Method\n",
    "1. Firth penalized logistic regression (no separability issues with the rare event)\n",
    "2. Stratified-by-race logit (route b) as sensitivity\n",
    "3. Stratified-by-race bootstrap (B=1000) for AME and OR CIs\n",
    "4. AUC by subgroup computed via Mann-Whitney U\n",
    "5. Predicted-probability curves and forest plot rendered with PIL\n",
    "\n"
   ]
